s and No:\n                      ©   “Are you tired?” “Yes,    / No, I’m not’\n                          “Will Bill be here tomorrow?” “Yes, he will. / No, he\n                      Oc\n                          “Is there a bus to the airport?” “Yes, there is. / No, there isn’t.”\n\n          Cc     We  use do/does for the simple present (see Units 6-7):\n                      ©         like hot weather, but Sue does. (= Sue likes hot weather)\n                      ©   Sue works hard, but | don’t. (= | don’t work hard)\n                      ©   “Do you enjoy your work?”  “Yes, | do.”\n                 We  use did for the simple past (see Unit 12):\n                      ©   a: Did you and Chris like the movie?\n                          B: | did, but Chris didn’t. (= | liked it, but Chris didn’t like it)\n                      Q                        “I did, too” (=| had a good time, too)\n                      ©   “Did it rain yesterday?” “No, it didn’t”\n\n\n                 ( You have? / Have you?, etc.                  neither do |, etc. > Unit 40", "char_count": 2998, "mean_conf": 86.09, "word_count": 400, "words": [{"text": "I'm", "x0": 518, "y0": 390, "x1": 563, "y1": 423, "conf": 93, "bold": false}, {"text": "not", "x0": 576, "y0": 394, "x1": 641, "y1": 423, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "tired.", "x0": 649, "y0": 389, "x1": 748, "y1": 422, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "She", "x0": 379, "y0": 1016, "x1": 446, "y1": 1053, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "isn’t", "x0": 461, "y0": 1016, "x1": 532, "y1": 1053, "conf": 89, "bold": false}, {"text": "tired,", "x0": 546, "y0": 1016, "x1": 640, "y1": 1056, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "but", "x0": 656, "y0": 1015, "x1": 719, "y1": 1051, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "he", "x0": 734, "y0": 1014, "x1": 782, "y1": 1051, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "is.", "x0": 797, "y0": 1015, "x1": 832, "y1": 1051, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "He", "x0": 1604, "y0": 1011, "x1": 165